	(text "Function: U7 translates TMS from FTDI3.3V to XEM1.8V.\nSource / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8305 A03,25Oct2023,\nJTAG sheet8/PDFp4: U504/C525/C526 -> U7/C40/C41.\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nSame SN74AXC1T45DBVR and two100nF values; topology unchanged.\nCodex redraw follows BRK row spacing and vertical bypass layout.\nRail names: USBJTAG_3.3V / XEM_1.8V; DGND renamed GND.\nTI SCES882E,Dec2023,pp3,18:\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74axc1t45.pdf\nDIR5=3.3V (A-to-B). PCB/powered operation remain unverified.\nV2 bypass part selection: same two100nF0402 positions; KEMET ->\nSamsung CL05B104KO5NNNC,16V X7R. No R or wire changes.\nSamsung Reference Sheet,9Apr2024,p1A/B:\nhttps://product.samsungsem.com/part/download.do?masterKey=CL05B104KO5NNN&type=specsheet"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 464.185 530.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3cc6698f-4e33-4a9c-9c8d-5445cc4730aa")
	)
	(text "Function: U5 translates TDI from FTDI3.3V to XEM1.8V.\nSource / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8305 A03,25Oct2023,\nJTAG sheet8/PDFp4: U502/C515/C516 -> U5/C36/C37.\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nSame SN74AXC1T45DBVR and two100nF values; topology unchanged.\nCodex redraw follows BRK row spacing and vertical bypass layout.\nRail names: USBJTAG_3.3V / XEM_1.8V; DGND renamed GND.\nTI SCES882E,Dec2023,pp3,18:\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/sn74axc1t45.pdf\nDIR5=3.3V (A-to-B). PCB/powered operation remain unverified.\nV2 bypass part selection: same two100nF0402 positions; KEMET ->\nSamsung CL05B104KO5NNNC,16V X7R. No R or wire changes.\nSamsung Reference Sheet,9Apr2024,p1A/B:\nhttps://product.samsungsem.com/part/download.do?masterKey=CL05B104KO5NNN&type=specsheet"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 464.185 464.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "41b15a73-a4be-4879-8c7b-e4358c7026cb")
	)
	(text "Function: U1 converts 12 V to the main carrier 3.3 V rail. R3/R4/C10 form its feedback network.\nTP2 probes 3.3 V after L1; TP3 probes 1.5 V. D3/R14 indicate voltage presence (about 0.3 mA\nnominal), not power-good status.\nU2 derives 1.5 V from 3.3 V when enabled by XEM_PG.\n\nSource / changes: Inherited TI-style TPS54429E circuit; V6 placement/routing is a Codex\nadaptation for RSA16. TI SLVSAS0 (February 2011), p. 5 RSA pin map, p. 14 Table 1 and p. 16\nFigure 16. Figure 16 shows PWP14; it is guidance, not an unchanged RSA layout.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps54429e.pdf\nR3 = 73.2 kohm, R4 = 22.1 kohm and C10 = 10 pF match the TI 3.3 V row. V6 L1 = 3.3 uH\ndiffered from that row's 2.2 uH. C3/C4 = 22 uF/100 nF, C8/C9 = 2 x 22 uF, R2 = 10 kohm VIN-to-EN\nare retained. No electrical value/netlist changes in V6.\nThermal-via implementation is documented in the V6 routing handoff. Effective capacitance,\nload/startup/stability, thermal behavior and assembly remain unqualified.\nTest/indicator branches were designed by Codex.\nV2 D3: Kingbright APT1608LZGCK replaces AA1608LCGSK; R14 stays 3 kohm.\nDSAN8392 V8B,8Apr2023,p1package/land/polarity,p2ratings,p3curves.\nhttps://www.kingbrightusa.com/images/catalog/spec/apt1608lzgck.pdf\nGreen hue570->525nm; nominal height0.60->0.75mm. Estimated0.30mA,\n~15mcd typical at3.3V from typical curves; not a bench measurement.\nR14: Vishay D/CRCW e3, document 20035 (0603, 1%, 0.1 W).\nhttps://www.vishay.com/docs/20035/dcrcwe3.pdf\nTP arrangement: TI SLVU444A, Rev. A, August 2021, p. 6, Table 4-1. LED pads follow the\nmanufacturer; courtyard/silk are Codex choices. Actual brightness and probe access remain\nunverified.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ug/slvu444a/slvu444a.pdf\nU2 V2: TLV75515PDRVR replaces DQN; OUT1/GND3/EN4/IN6/EP7; NC2/5 visibly open.\nTI SBVS320D Sep2024 p3 Fig4-4/Table4-1; DRV0006A 4222173/C Nov2025, PDF pp41-43.\nC11/C12 = 4.7 uF and R5 = 100 kohm retained; Codex local reroute/paste and mask +0.05 mm.\nEffective capacitance, actual bank load, thermal behavior and assembly remain unqualified.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tlv755p.pdf\nThermal-via reference: RSA0016B drawing 4219093/A, August 2021, datasheet PDF pp. 23-24; TI QFN\nand SON PCB Attachment, SLUA271C, December 2023, section 3.4.1 p. 7. Opposite-face tenting and\nthe retained nine-window stencil require assembly/voiding review.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/an/slua271b/slua271b.pdf\nV2 exact commodity selections retain all nominal R/C values and connections:\nR3/R4=Yageo RC0402FR-0773K2L/0722K1L; C4=Samsung CL05B104KA5NNNC\n(100nF25V X7R); C5=CL10A105KA8NNNC (1uF25V X5R),\nC6=CL05B332KB5NNNC (3.3nF50V X7R), C7=CL05B104KO5NNNC(100nF16V X7R),\nC8/C9=CL31B226KPHNNNE(22uF10V X7R), C10=CL05C100JB5NNNC(10pF50V C0G).\nSamsung Reference Sheets,Apr/May2024,p1A/B; exact per-part datasheets\nare populated on each symbol. No other rail or enable topology changes.\nC3 V4: TDK C3216X5R1V226MTJ00E (C342620) is the same device as\ncatalog C3216X5R1V226M160AC;22uF35V X5R1206,lands/wires retained.\nTDK Ceramic Capacitor Supply Status Update,12Jan2023,p12:\nhttps://media.futureelectronics.com/PCN/95306_SPCN.PDF\nV7 (Claude, 24 Nov): +3V3 also feeds ASIC_Rails, 0.3 A typ/1.1 A worst of 4.5 A; U2 feeds 4 VCCO banks.\nU2 load est. <60 mA of 500 mA (33 outputs DRIVE 4 SLOW + pulls). +3V3 Cout ~87 uF nom. (C42 DNP) > TI 68 uF.\nU1 LCSC C2859852 (4 left) -> C1880068 TPS54429ERSAT: same TI part, 250-pc reel, same RSA QFN-16 land.\nV7 sch V2: L1 XAL5030-332MEC C5342047 (-7 orderable) -> XAL5030-222MEC C920280 (2.2 uH):\nTI SLVSAS0 p.14 Table 1 3.3 V row; same XAL5030 size code, footprint unchanged. Coilcraft\nDoc 908-1 rev 02/26/26 p.1: Isat 9.2 A (30% drop), Irms 7.2 A, DCR 14.5 mohm max."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 358.775 295.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.20 1.20)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "53f605c8-128c-48ef-96eb-2ab852b703d3")
	)
