		(uuid "9ab78d80-2d91-4fba-9dba-40337b8b3fda")
	)
	(text "Function: J3 receives barrel-jack12V. C2 stores input charge; C1 bypasses XEM12V. D1 shunts transients and clamps a reversed adapter.\nR1/D2 indicate input voltage; TP1/TP7 provide12V/GND probe access.\n\nSource / changes: Inherited carrier input structure; original author/reference is not established.\nV6 changed placement/copper, retaining values/connections; this is not a TI protection reference design.\nV3 C2: Panasonic EEEFTE221XAL (C1881633) replaces EEE-FTE221XAP with the FT[HF] configuration.\nSame220uF/25V/20%,600mArms100kHz,ESR160mOhmmax,2000h105C; body6.3x7.7mm,H8.0max.\nPanasonic FT[HF] RDE0000C1269,1Sep2025,pp1-2: dimensions,frequency factors,exact220uF/25V row.\nhttps://industrial.panasonic.com/cdbs/www-data/pdf/RDE0000/RDE0000C1269.pdf\nDME0000COL48,30Jan2026,p2 standardD8:3.2x1.6mm pads,gap1.8mm. Geometry/polarity/wires unchanged.\nhttps://industrial.panasonic.com/cdbs/www-data/pdf/RDE0000/DME0000COL48.pdf\nCodex retains the KiCad-derived body/courtyard and illustrative model; actual ripple/fit remain unverified.\nJ3: Same Sky PJ-102AH manufacturer product drawing and recommended PCB layout.\nhttps://www.sameskydevices.com/product/resource/pj-102ah.pdf\nSchematic V9 D1 (Claude, 26 Nov 2026): Littelfuse SMBJ15A (JLC C83846) replaces Diodes SMBJ15CA-13-F (C135047).\nChanged: one direction instead of bidirectional, and turned round: cathode (pin 1) on +12V, anode on GND.\nA reversed adapter now forward-biases D1 (about -1 V at the input); no fuse, it relies on the adapter current limit.\nSame 15 V standoff, 16.7-18.5 V breakdown at 1 mA, 24.4 V clamp at 24.6 A, 600 W (Littelfuse product page):\nhttps://www.littelfuse.com/products/overvoltage-protection/tvs-diodes/surface-mount/smbj/smbj15a\nSame DO-214AA (SMB) package on the unchanged D_SMB footprint. Not verified: the Littelfuse land pattern and\nforward surge rating (datasheet PDF could not be opened); earlier part: https://www.diodes.com/part/view/SMBJ15CA\nU1 VIN absmax20V: TI SLVSAS0,Feb2011,p2. Transient/reverse-input/supply/load limits remain unqualified.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps54429e.pdf\nCodex test pads: TI SLVU444A,RevA,Aug2021,p6 Table4-1 precedent; local1.5mm pads,no paste.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ug/slvu444a/slvu444a.pdf\nV2 C1: Samsung CL05B104KA5NNNC,100nF25V X7R0402,same C/rating/size as reference-only Taiyo.\nSamsung Reference Sheet,9Apr2024,p1A/B (C1 Datasheet). Stacked probe/assembly access is unverified."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171.45 234.95 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.2 1.2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a06d54a6-4b70-44db-8173-de6f9eea00e1")
	)
	(text "Function: D4 shows rawUSB5V; R15=6.8kohm\nretains about0.47mA typical LED load.\nTP5=rawUSB5V; TP6=FTDI3.3V; TP8=GND.\nSource / changes: Codex probe/LED branch;\nV2 APT1608LSYCK/J3-PRV replaces AA1608LSYSK.\nR15 value and all electrical connections retained.\nKingbright DSAN8389,V5B,6Jan2021,p1land/\npolarity,p2ratings,p3typical curves:\nhttps://www.kingbrightusa.com/\nimages/catalog/SPEC/\nAPT1608LSYCK-J3-PRV.pdf\nSymmetric0.8x0.8mm pads at+/-0.825mm;\nK1/A2 retained. Yellow590nm; height0.75mm\n(general+/-0.1mm). Typical~6mcd at5V\nis estimated, not measured. USB suspend\ncurrent and assembled brightness remain to test.\nR15: Vishay doc20035,0603,1%,0.1W.\nhttps://www.vishay.com/docs/20035/dcrcwe3.pdf\nTestpads: TI SLVU444A,RevA,p6,Table4-1.\nhttps://www.ti.com/lit/ug/slvu444a/slvu444a.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.5 403.225 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.15 1.15)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d8e274ac-bac6-4aa6-80f2-f966837b3ab2")
	)
