	(text_box "1. Function: MC1 (banks 64, 84) and MC2 (banks 85, 86) carry the 121 LVCMOS15 lines of the 4K head to the router plugs J5/J6 (sheet Router_Interface) by global labels: 88 ASIC outputs into the FPGA (DATA1-8, READ, SYNC and CLK32MHz_Out of ASIC1-8) and 33 FPGA outputs (BOARD1/3 clocks, SPI clocks, latches and data, the seven *_SHARED controls). +1V5 from U2 (XEM_PG-gated TLV75515) feeds VCCO_64 (MC1.2/4) and now also VCCO_84 (MC1.1/3), VCCO_85 (MC2.37/39) and VCCO_86 (MC2.41/43).\n\n2. Source / changes: Pins from pin table V3 (with its 24 Nov review fixes), XEM8305_PIN_TABLE_V3.csv and Carrier_V7_XEM8305_V3.xdc (24 Nov 2026). Schematic V3 (Claude, approved by Howard 24 Nov) changes only the XEM side, re-derived by board geometry: each net's MC1/MC2 pin and FPGA ball (ASIC5/6/8 bank 64, ASIC7 bank 84, ASIC1/3 bank 85, ASIC2/4 bank 86); router contract PIN_MAP_B_V2, net and XDC port names and parts unchanged. Checked against PIN_MAP_B_V2 and the Opal Kelly pin list with 0 differences (inventory/I3_interface_spec_V3.csv). Opal Kelly XEM8305 Pin List (web table, MC1/MC2/MC3 rows, accessed 24 Nov 2026), https://pins.opalkelly.com/pin_list/XEM8305 ; Opal Kelly XEM8305 Expansion Connectors (VCCO supply pins; web page accessed 24 Nov 2026), https://docs.opalkelly.com/xem8305/expansion-connectors/ ; AMD UltraScale Architecture SelectIO Resources UG571 (HTML edition as served 24 Nov 2026, LVCMOS15 standard, VCCO 1.5 V), https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug571-ultrascale-selectio ; AMD UG572 v1.11, Global Clock Inputs (the eight returned CLK32MHz lines sit on GC/HDGC P pins), https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug572-ultrascale-clocking (section Global Clock Inputs). Changed from Carrier V6 by Claude: old LDO plugs J1 (LDO_50DS) and J2 (LDO_24DS) removed with their 23 labels, 4 power symbols and 47 no-connect flags; the 23 V6 MC1 labels renamed to V7 nets and 98 MC1/MC2 no-connect flags replaced by labels; VCCO_84/85/86 (6 pins) moved from no-connect to +1V5; the MC2 ground buses split into one GND symbol per pin (same GND net) so no label crosses a wire; MC3 moved 40.64 mm right and the whole V6 drawing 30.48 mm right. MC1.87 (VRP), MC1.89 (VREF_64) and the two spare I/O pins MC2.19 (J9, bank 85) and MC2.22 (E11, bank 85 HDGC P, kept for a later clock) stay unconnected. MC3 (XEM8305 MGT socket) carries only DGND here: its MGT, REFCLK and SYSMON pins stay open, unchanged from V6 apart from the 40.64 mm move. MC2.8 VBATT stays open as on V6 and on the Opal Kelly BRK8305 (pin list column BRK8305 Pin is empty for VBATT). U2 load estimate (Claude): 33 outputs at DRIVE 4 / SLEW SLOW, about 33 x 20 pF x 1.5 V x 32 MHz = 32 mA, plus about 2 mA into the 10k pulls, under 60 mA of 500 mA. XEM8305_PG is a 1.8 V signal that goes high once the FPGA rails are good, and Opal Kelly asks for VCCO only after that (Opal Kelly, Powering the XEM8305, https://docs.opalkelly.com/xem8305/powering-the-xem8305/ , accessed 24 Nov 2026); the ASIC rails now also wait for it (U21, sheet ASIC_Rails). Schematic V4 (25 Nov 2026) adds C69 (4.7 uF 10 V C23733) and C70 (100 nF 16 V C1525) directly on the MC2 +1V5 bus for local VCCO_85/86 decoupling beside banks 85/86 (45 mm from U2/C11). Unverified: the XDC is not run in Vivado for this board (5 chips capture in HD banks 84/85/86, which have no IDELAY/ISERDES)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
